        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the remainder when $x^2-7x+12$ is divided by its factor $(x-3)$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "PSF: Product $12$, Sum $-7$, Factors $-3$ and $-4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-7x+12&=(x-3)(x-4)\\end{align*}$$\nA factor divides the expression exactly, so the remainder is $0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "backfill-factor-theorem-2-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The polynomial $P(x)$ is written as $P(x)=(x+3)Q(x)$.\nWhat is the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x+3)$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+3)Q(x)+0\\end{align*}$$\nThe divisor is $(x+3)$ and $(x+3)$ is a factor of $P(x)$, so the remainder is $0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
